\uses{lem:combined-point-marginal-projection-estimates, lem:qld-4-10,
 def:symmetric-equivalents, fact:agreement}
This is an auxiliary statement for an arbitrary joint point witness whose
three squared-distance bounds are at most $t$. Fix directed opposite
placements, and denote the placed effects by $Q_{a,b}^{x,z}$ on the first
placement and $X_a^x,Z_b^z$ on the second. With uniform independent $x,z$,
\[
 \E_{x,z}\sum_{a,b}\|(Q_{a,b}^{x,z}-X_a^xQ_{a,b}^{x,z})\psi\|^2\leq t,
 \qquad
 \E_{x,z}\sum_{a,b}\|(Q_{a,b}^{x,z}-Z_b^zQ_{a,b}^{x,z})\psi\|^2\leq t.
\]
The squared distances of $\sum_bQ_{a,b}^{x,z}$ from $X_a^x$, and of
$\sum_aQ_{a,b}^{x,z}$ from $Z_b^z$, are each at most $4t$ after averaging.
The joint self-consistency defect is at most $t$ under the same uniform law.
These assertions retain $t$; they do not yet assert the marginal comparisons
with evaluated line measurements under the line-point law.
\end{lemma}
\begin{proof}
\leanok
Use the ordered $XZ$ comparison for absorption of $X$ and the ordered $ZX$
comparison for absorption of $Z$. For the X marginal use the preceding
lemma with the Z projectors and $D=X_a^x$; for the Z marginal interchange
the two bases. Opposite placements commute, and projectivity of the joint
measurement gives orthogonality within each marginal fiber. Average the
resulting inequalities and use the corresponding supplied error bounds.
Joint projectivity and the agreement identity convert its supplied
squared-distance self-consistency bound into a consistency-defect bound.
\end{proof}

